      "latex_extracted": null,
      "source_page_number": null,
      "source_image_index": null,
      "ownership": "unknown"
    },
    "parts": [],
    "answer_text": "The Poet believes that his poetry cannot be destroyed by the forces of nature or wars. It will be read by coming generations. It will be remembered till posterity. It cannot be forgotten. Even Godly powers of Mars will not have a devastating effect on his rhymes. It will survive in the hearts of its lovers. In this way, the poet is quite sure of the immortality of his poetry. The poet’s extreme optimism and deep faith in the power of love is revealed in these lines.",
    "answer_latex": null,
    "steps": [],
    "final_answer": "Thus, the poet's faith in the immortality of his poetry reflects his optimism and belief in love.",
